The font files in this directory are vendored so the settings page can offer
them to any browser, not only to machines that happen to have them installed.
All three are licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1, which
permits redistribution as part of a larger work.

  3270-Regular.ttf        "IBM 3270", the IBM 3270 terminal font digitised by
                          Ricardo Banffy.
                          https://github.com/rbanffy/3270font

  FiraMono-Regular.ttf    "Fira Mono" by Carrois Apostrophe / Mozilla.
                          https://github.com/mozilla/Fira

  IBMPlexMono-Regular.ttf "IBM Plex Mono" by IBM.
                          https://github.com/IBM/plex

The full licence text is at https://scripts.sil.org/OFL. In summary: the fonts
may be used, studied, modified and redistributed freely, they may not be sold on
their own, and a modified version may not use the reserved font names.

The other fonts the settings page offers are not shipped. They are named in a
font stack and resolve to whatever the browser's own machine has, falling back
to its default monospace face.
